    "id": "train-6668",
    "question": "Winston had 10 gallons of gas in his car’s gas tank. He drives to the store and uses 6 gallons of gas. Then he drives to the doctor’s office and uses 2 gallons of gas. If the tank can hold up to 12 gallons of gas, how many gallons of gas will Winston need to refill the entire tank?",
    "gold": "10",
    "answer": "After driving to the store and doctor’s office, Winston has 10 - 6 - 2 = <<10-6-2=2>>2 gallons of gas left in the tank\nTo refill the entire tank, Winston needs 12 - 2 = <<12-2=10>>10 gallons of gas\n#### 10"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many gallons of gas Winston will need to refill his car's gas tank, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of gas used.\n2. Subtract the total amount of gas used from the initial amount of gas in the tank.\n3. Determine how much gas is needed to refill the tank to its full capacity.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total amount of gas used.\nWinston used 6 gallons to drive to the store and 2 gallons to drive to the doctor's office. Therefore, the total amount of gas used is:\n\\[ 6 + 2 = 8 \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\nStep 2: Subtract the total amount of gas used from the initial amount of gas in the tank.\nWinston initially had 10 gallons of gas in his tank. After using 8 gallons, the amount of gas left in the tank is:\n\\[ 10 - 8 = 2 \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\nStep 3: Determine how much gas is needed to refill the tank to its full capacity.\nThe tank can hold up to 12 gallons of gas. Since there are 2 gallons left in the tank, the amount of gas needed to refill the tank is:\n\\[ 12 - 2 = 10 \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of gallons of gas Winston will need to refill the entire tank is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
